title: "Computational Time Machine: Accelerated AI Civilizations for Compressing Technological R&D Time"
type: article
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-09-10
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22687555"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22687555"
authors:
  - given-names: "Nickolay"
    family-names: "Gorlanov"
abstract: >-
  A research concept proposing a persistent generational AI R&D ecosystem,
  Civilization-in-the-Loop (CitL), designed to test whether independently
  validated discoveries can compound across AI research generations and
  compress technological R&D time. The proposal introduces the Technological
  Time Compression Ratio (TTCR), branching technological futures, and
  real-world validation through robotic experimentation.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - automated AI researcher
  - recursive self-improvement
  - agentic research
  - AI civilization
  - technological time compression
  - Civilization-in-the-Loop
  - TTCR
